class.description:
A transport is everything the session knows about one [MultiplayerPeer] class. It builds a peer, lists what that class can reach, probes an address, and adopts a peer a game built itself. A session makes one instance the first time it needs one, and a class registered through [method NetwMultiplayer.transport_register] or [method NetwConnectHandle.register_transport] returns what it is called before any instance exists.
A transport is keyed by [method peer_class] and never by a URL scheme, and [method recognizes_peer] is what decides whether a peer a game built and assigned itself belongs to this transport. A transport that has to exchange its own connection details before a peer can be built, as WebRTC does, subclasses [NetwWebRTCSignaler] for that half.
[codeblock]
class_name RelayTransport
extends NetwTransport

func _peer_class() -> StringName:
    return &"RelayMultiplayerPeer"

func _host_settings() -> Dictionary:
    return {region = "eu"}

func _make_peer(ticket: RID, mode: int, address: String,
        settings: Dictionary) -> void:
    report(ticket, &"handshake", "Reaching the relay...", 0.5)
    var peer := RelayMultiplayerPeer.new()
    var err: Error = await peer.connect_async(address, settings.region)
    if err != OK:
        fail(ticket, ERR_CANT_CONNECT, "relay rejected")
        return
    _room = peer.room
    deliver(ticket, peer)

func _cancel_peer_creation(ticket: RID) -> void:
    if ticket == _building:
        _building = RID()

func _join_address() -> String:
    return _room

func _ready() -> void:
    Netw.connection(self).register_transport(RelayTransport)
[/codeblock]
[method _make_peer] and [method _probe] return [code]void[/code] and report through [method deliver], [method deliver_probe] and [method fail], called once from any frame. A [code]GDVIRTUAL[/code] with a typed return coerces a suspended coroutine to an empty value and reports success, so a seam that returned its result directly would return nothing the instant it first awaited; a [code]void[/code] seam discards that empty return harmlessly and the coroutine keeps running on whatever signals it awaits. A seam that reports neither is caught by the deadline [method timeout_hint] declares, unless that hint is negative.
Every report carries the [RID] ticket the seam was handed, and an implementation that awaits captures that ticket in a local before the first [code]await[/code] rather than reading it from a field. A report under a retired ticket is discarded, which is what keeps a slow provider returning an abandoned request from publishing its peer under a newer one's identity.
A transport belongs to the session that registered it, and a peer class is unique within one: a second registration of the same script returns the standing one, and a different script for a class the session already registers is rejected. [method NetwMultiplayer.transport_register] carries that law, and [method NetwMultiplayer.transport_unregister] is how a registration is replaced or withdrawn.

method.description:
Override to return the fields a join form asks for, in the shape [method _host_settings] returns, and [method NetwMultiplayer.transport_create_peer] reads them back the same way. A transport that overrides nothing offers no fields.
Return settings used by [method _make_peer] in [constant NetwMultiplayer.TRANSPORT_MODE_CLIENT]. Client and host settings may contain the same keys.
[codeblock]
func _client_settings() -> Dictionary:
    return {region = "eu"}

func _host_settings() -> Dictionary:
    var settings := _client_settings()
    settings.max_players = 32
    return settings
[/codeblock]

Publishes what [method _browse] found: one row per entry of [param addresses], titled by the matching entry of [param names] and described by the matching [NetwServerInfo] of [param infos] where one is known. The three arrays are read in step, and a short [param names] or [param infos] simply leaves those rows untitled or unobserved.
[codeblock]
func _browse() -> void:
    var lobbies := await _sdk.search()
    var addresses := PackedStringArray()
    var names := PackedStringArray()
    var infos: Array[NetwServerInfo] = []
    for lobby in lobbies:
        addresses.append(lobby.id)
        names.append(lobby.name)
        infos.append(_info_of(lobby))
    publish_targets(_peer_class(), addresses, names, infos)
[/codeblock]
